# November 28, 2026: state hospitals and asylums of Michigan, Wisconsin and Minnesota, a batch of the themed pass on
# historic state hospitals. Already on the map and left alone: the Northern Michigan Asylum (Building 50, Traverse City)
# and the Kalamazoo State Hospital's water tower and gatehouse.
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia (Clinton Valley Center, Eloise, Mendota Mental Health Institute, Winnebago
# Mental Health Institute, Minnesota Security Hospital, St. Peter State Hospital Museum, Fergus Falls Regional Treatment
# Center, Anoka Metro Regional Treatment Center, Dodge Correctional Institution); the Park Service's National Register
# records and forms for the Southern Wisconsin Home (91001394), the Central State Hospital at Waupun (91001395), the
# Wisconsin Memorial Hospital (88002183), the St. Peter Center Building (86002117) and the Willmar Hospital Farm for
# Inebriates (86001535); the Wisconsin Historical Society's property records for Chippewa Falls; SAH Archipedia
# (Newberry, Fergus Falls); MNopedia (Anoka, Rochester, Willmar); KirkbrideBuildings.com; Asylum Projects; HMdb (the
# Chippewa Falls marker); the Cultural Landscape Foundation and WUWM (Sanctuary Woods); the Quarry Hill Nature Center;
# Placeography and the Living New Deal (Moose Lake); the Minnesota and Michigan corrections departments; the Wisconsin
# Department of Health Services; Winnebago County (Asylum Point); and news pieces from the AP, Audacy (WWJ), the
# Mankato Free Press group (New Ulm Journal), the Star Tribune, the Perham Focus, KVRR, Newberry News and WKFR.
# Pins: OpenStreetMap points, Wikipedia coordinates, address points and the HMdb marker position, each looked at on the
# aerial (see PIN_NOTES).
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W
BATCH={'key':'asylum_grlk_pmpr','label':'State hospitals and asylums, Michigan, Wisconsin and Minnesota','added':'2026-11-28 07:26'}
